<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 656–659</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abdallah ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Sarh was an Arab commander and governor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> from about 645 to 656 under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> Uthman, his foster-brother. In 652 he besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/old-dongola">Old Dongola</a>, capital of the Nubian kingdom of Makuria, but could not take it and concluded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baqt">Baqt</a>, a treaty that governed Egyptian–Nubian relations for six centuries. He also led raids into north <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> and commanded at the naval victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-the-masts">Battle of the Masts</a>.</p></div>
